#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:1
msgid "Feature Name: feature-documentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:2
msgid "Start Date: 2023-09-09"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:3
msgid ""
"RFC PR: [rust-lang/rfcs#3485](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3485)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:4
msgid ""
"Rust Issue: [rust-lang/cargo#17445](https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/"
"issues/17445)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:7
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:11
msgid ""
"This RFC describes a new key under `features` in `Cargo.toml` for "
"documentation. This will allow Cargo to display this information to the user "
"and provide a way for `rustdoc` to eventually render this data (how this is "
"rendered is outside the scope of this RFC)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:16
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:18
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[features.serde]\n"
"enables = []\n"
"doc = \"enable support for serialization and deserialization via serde\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:24
msgid ""
"Please see the parent meta RFC for background information: [`feature-"
"metadata`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3416)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:26
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:30
msgid ""
"Cargo features have become extremely widely used, with many crates having at "
"least some level of configuration and larger crates winding up with tens of "
"gates. Despite being a first class component of crate structure, they suffer "
"from a documentation problem: users need to maintain documentation separate "
"from feature definition, typically a manually-created table within API docs."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:36
msgid ""
"This RFC proposes adding feature documentation to `Cargo.toml`, which will "
"allow for keeping feature definitions and documentation together."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:39
msgid "Guide-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:43
msgid ""
"A new `doc` key will be allowed within a feature's table. This key provides "
"a markdown docstring describing the feature. The first paragraph will be "
"treated as a summary, and should be suitable to display standalone without "
"the rest of the description."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:48
msgid ""
"Don't include the name of the feature in the summary; tools will typically "
"already display this documentation alongside the name of the feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:51
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[features]\n"
"# Feature without documentation\n"
"foo = []\n"
"\n"
"# Short documentation comment\n"
"bar = { enables = [\"foo\"], doc = \"simple docstring here\"}\n"
"\n"
"# Tables are preferred for longer descriptions\n"
"[features.corge]\n"
"enables = [\"bar\", \"baz\"]\n"
"doc = \"\"\"\n"
"The first paragraph is a short summary, which might be displayed "
"standalone.\n"
"This could be a longer description of this feature\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:68
msgid ""
"See [`feature-metadata`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3416) for "
"information about `enables`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:70
msgid "Reference-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:74
msgid ""
"The new `doc` key accepts markdown-flavored text, and should be thought of "
"as the equivalent to a `#[doc(...)]` attribute. Like doc comments, the first "
"paragraph should be treated as a summary. Intra-doc link support is not "
"included in this RFC, so they should not be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:79
msgid ""
"There is nothing in this RFC that cargo **must** do with this action, since "
"it is mainly intended for the consumption of `rustdoc` or `docs.rs`. "
"However, it can be used for general diagnostic information such as during "
"`cargo add` or a possible `cargo info` command. A sample application with "
"`cargo add`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:102
msgid ""
"_(features like `aho-corasick`, `memchr`, or `use_std` would likely be "
"`public = false` since they aren't listed on the crate landing page)_"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:105
msgid ""
"Any tools that want the information in `doc` will require access to the "
"manifest. Adding this information to the index was decided against due to "
"concerns about bloat, but this is further discussed in [future possibilities]"
"(#future-possibilities)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:110
msgid "Drawbacks"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:114
msgid "Added complexity to Cargo."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:115
msgid "Exact implementation details do add test surface area"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:116
msgid "A markdown parser is required to properly parse the `doc` field."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:117
msgid ""
"Docstrings can be lengthy, adding noise to `Cargo.toml`. This could "
"potentially be solved with the below mentioned `doc-file` key."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:119
msgid ""
"When rendering features in documentation, this RFC does not specify any way "
"for `rustdoc` to get the information it requires. This will require separate "
"design work."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:122
msgid ""
"Unlike with the [`document-features`](https://crates.io/crates/document-"
"features) crate there is no way to group features into sections or have a "
"user-specified layout"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:125
msgid ""
"Users cannot control features ordering in documentation since the TOML "
"specification defines table keys as unordered."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:128
msgid "Rationale and alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:132
msgid ""
"To avoid increasing the size of the registry index, this does not add `doc` "
"to a package's index entry. This means a `.crate` file must be downloaded "
"and extracted to access the features."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:135
msgid ""
"Feature descriptions could be specified somewhere in Rust source files. This "
"has the downside of creating multiple sources of truth on features."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:137
msgid ""
"Cargo could parse doc comments in `Cargo.toml`, like the `document-features` "
"crate (linked below)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:140
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"# RFC proposal\n"
"foo = { enables = [], doc = \"foo feature\" }\n"
"\n"
"# Alternative equivalent using doc comments\n"
"## foo feature\n"
"foo = []\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:149
msgid ""
"This was decided against as part of this RFC because it would mean that TOML-"
"compliant parsers (including anything `serde`\\-based) would be insufficient "
"to extract all information in the manifest, requiring custom deserialization "
"of the fields via a format-preserving parser. This differs from "
"documentation in Rust source as the doc-comment behavior is described "
"specified within the grammar with parsers supporting extracting those "
"elements."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:157
msgid "Prior art"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:161
msgid ""
"There is an existing crate that uses TOML comments to create a features "
"table: <https://docs.rs/document-features/latest/document_features/>"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:163
msgid ""
"`docs.rs` displays a feature table, but it is fairly limited. If features "
"start with `_`, they are hidden from this table ([example](https://docs.rs/"
"crate/regex/latest/features))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:166
msgid ""
"`lib.rs` extracts feature documentation from `Cargo.toml` and source "
"([example](https://lib.rs/crates/regex/features))"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:169
msgid "Unresolved questions"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:173
msgid ""
"What is the best name for the manifest key? `doc` was chosen for consistency "
"with `#[doc(...)]`, but `package.description` and `package.documentation` (a "
"URL) also exist as precedent."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:176
msgid ""
"How should this be exposed in `cargo metadata` output? One possibility is to "
"extend the existing `features` entry with a parallel structure:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:180
msgid "\"features\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:181 src/3485-feature-documentation.md:182
#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:185 src/3485-feature-documentation.md:186
msgid "\"foo\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:182 src/3485-feature-documentation.md:186
msgid "\"bar\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:184
msgid "\"features_v2\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:186
msgid "\"enables\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:186
msgid "\"doc\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:186
msgid "\"simple docstring for bar\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:190
msgid "Future possibilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:194
msgid "Rustdoc can build on this to show feature documentation."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:196
msgid ""
"If this RFC gets stabilized before any corresponding change in rustdoc, its "
"documentation should highlight that rustdoc may parse the description and "
"support intra-doc links in the future, but not at the current time. Users "
"need to be aware of this potential incompatibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:200
msgid ""
"At some point, the decision to not include `doc` in the index could be "
"reevaluated. Including only the first (summary) line of `doc` could be a "
"possibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:203
msgid ""
"`cargo add` can show the `doc` and `deprecated` summary with the listed "
"features."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:205
msgid ""
"[`cargo-info`](https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/issues/948) can use this "
"information to provide feature descriptions."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:206
msgid "crates-io could be updated to render feature documentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:207
msgid ""
"Feature documentation could be allowed in a separate markdown file. For "
"convenience, markdown anchors could be used to specify a section, so "
"multiple features can share the same file. This could be a good option for "
"features requiring long descriptions."
msgstr ""

#: src/3485-feature-documentation.md:212
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"foo = { enables = [], doc-file = \"features.md#foo\" }\n"
"bar = { enables = [], doc-file = \"features.md#bar\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
